      "start_seconds": 0.8,
      "end_seconds": 5.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Uh, good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.49,
      "end_seconds": 11.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "that's fine, sit down tell me why you came"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 15.0,
      "end_seconds": 25.83,
      "duration_seconds": 10.83,
      "text": "good morning, doctor. I came along to help out. It's, It's been feeling faint, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.54,
      "end_seconds": 30.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.7,
      "end_seconds": 35.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Around about a month, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 36.99,
      "end_seconds": 41.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "I think it's been nearer about two months, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.97,
      "end_seconds": 47.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "okay, so roughly one to two months is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.91,
      "end_seconds": 50.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "That sounds about right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.84,
      "end_seconds": 62.33,
      "duration_seconds": 9.49,
      "text": "tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.47,
      "end_seconds": 71.9,
      "duration_seconds": 8.43,
      "text": "it comes and goes. Mostly severe. Work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.99,
      "end_seconds": 75.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.84,
      "end_seconds": 96.19,
      "duration_seconds": 17.35,
      "text": "it usually comes with a very fast heartbeat the, The very fast heartbeat? That's been for about four days with very fast heartbeat, about a eight out of ten i've been sweating too"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.16,
      "end_seconds": 100.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.19,
      "end_seconds": 113.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "keep your arm relaxed for me.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.91,
      "end_seconds": 141.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "okay: temperature is 37.0 degrees, saturation 99 percent, pulse 97. And blood pressure 98 over 60."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.81,
      "end_seconds": 146.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Right, could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.65,
      "end_seconds": 149.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "look straight ahead"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.84,
      "end_seconds": 172.61,
      "duration_seconds": 6.77,
      "text": "your pulse is over one hundred and eighty and your blood pressure is low"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.99,
      "end_seconds": 177.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "All finished, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.34,
      "end_seconds": 196.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Any fever, cough or leg swelling at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.86,
      "end_seconds": 200.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "No, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.71,
      "end_seconds": 205.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "So, any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.53,
      "end_seconds": 208.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "no, joints are fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.16,
      "end_seconds": 212.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.96,
      "end_seconds": 214.95,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.0,
      "end_seconds": 218.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.38,
      "end_seconds": 227.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "just a bunion operation, six years ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.27,
      "end_seconds": 231.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.88,
      "end_seconds": 236.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Um, my father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.33,
      "end_seconds": 245.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.03,
      "end_seconds": 259.81,
      "duration_seconds": 13.78,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts. I do a yoga class on Thursdays. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.02,
      "end_seconds": 264.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.4,
      "end_seconds": 269.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "I've had heart disease for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.44,
      "end_seconds": 271.28,
      "duration_seconds": 0.84,
      "text": "I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.18,
      "end_seconds": 276.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.67,
      "end_seconds": 286.48,
      "duration_seconds": 8.81,
      "text": "Okay, I can see high blood pressure in your file as well. Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.91,
      "end_seconds": 291.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "no, I've never reacted to anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.02,
      "end_seconds": 297.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "let's run through your medicines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.07,
      "end_seconds": 308.03,
      "duration_seconds": 9.96,
      "text": "I take ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning i'd been on telmisartan, not any more though, I stopped"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.34,
      "end_seconds": 323.28,
      "duration_seconds": 13.94,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, this looks most like a dangerous fast heart rhythm. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.13,
      "end_seconds": 327.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.06,
      "end_seconds": 348.54,
      "duration_seconds": 18.48,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a dangerous fast heart rhythm is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've been feeling faint, severe, and no cough or leg swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.95,
      "end_seconds": 351.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.34,
      "end_seconds": 368.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "we should do an urgent ECG for fast heart rhythm"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.95,
      "end_seconds": 371.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "How long will it take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.32,
      "end_seconds": 395.73,
      "duration_seconds": 22.41,
      "text": "we should do blood tests for arrhythmia lie flat, I am calling the emergency team and preparing to shock the heart don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day i'm gonna send a referral to the emergency team do get help quickly if the symptoms get worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.51,
      "end_seconds": 399.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Okay, I'll look out for that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.12,
      "end_seconds": 404.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Please come and and see me straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 406.42,
      "end_seconds": 407.12,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "right"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 408.08,
      "end_seconds": 410.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.62,
      "end_seconds": 415.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
